        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Paulownia, Dendromecon\n- Taxonomy: genera, species counts, plant families, native range\n\nFacts:\n- Paulownia is a genus of flowering plants with six to 17 species, depending on the taxonomic authority.\n- Paulownia belongs to the family Paulowniaceae and is related to, and sometimes included in, Scrophulariaceae.\n- Dendromecon, known as the tree poppy, is a genus of one or two species of shrubs to small trees.\n- Dendromecon is native to California and northern Baja California.",
